# Build output. The compiler writes here; nothing in it is a source, and a stale class file
# next to a fresh source is exactly how a fixed guard stops being fixed.
out/

# Runtime state. employees.dat holds password records, audit.log holds every authentication
# attempt, throttle.log holds the failure counters; all three are owner-private (0600) by
# design and none of them belongs in a repository, a backup ticket or a diff.
*.dat
*.dat.lock
*.log
*.log.lock

# TLS material. A keystore and its password file must never be committed together, and a
# keystore must never be committed at all even without the password.
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.password
*.key
*.pem

# The real config, as opposed to the committed .example. An operator's copy names absolute
# paths and may accumulate a value someone thought was harmless.
portal.properties
config/local.properties

# Scratch space used by the mutation battery (tools/mutate.py) and the test suites.
qmut*/
*.tmp
